ollerIntervalInMilliSeconds","properties":null,"required":false,"type":"integer","values":null,"valuesSource":"definition"},{"addressByName":false,"allowUserProperties":false,"allowUserValue":true,"defaultValue":20,"description":"Uses data partitions to read data from the database. This setting has the largest impact on overall indexing time. As such, SAS recommends changing this setting if you need to improve performance. This should be set high, but not so high that it causes memory consumption or resource issues. Consider whether you need extra performance to handle your workloads before increasing this setting. A suggested tuning exercise when resourcing issues are hit is to reduce this setting to 5 or 10 and then gradually increase it until you strike a balance between stability and performance.Note: Each instance of the Indexer contains its own set of workers. As a result, you might typically choose to increase the number of Indexer instances rather than increase the worker count.","label":"","list":false,"name":"workers.dataIndexer.numberOfWorkers","properties":null,"required":false,"type":"integer","values":null,"valuesSource":"definition"},{"addressByName":false,"allowUserProperties":false,"allowUserValue":true,"defaultValue":10,"description":"Removes data partition descriptors from the queue. This worker has a very simple job and leaving the default setting is recommended.","label":"","list":false,"name":"workers.dataIndexerLauncher.numberOfWorkers","properties":null,"required":false,"type":"integer","values":null,"valuesSource":"definition"},{"addressByName":false,"allowUserProperties":false,"allowUserValue":true,"defaultValue":10,"description":"Adds data partition descriptors to the queue. Each Data Partitioner worker can produce several partitions. SAS recommends setting the number of workers larger than that configured for Data Partitioner.","label":"","list":false,"name":"workers.dataPartitionInitializer.numberOfWorkers","properties":null,"required":f